# The Other Ninety (o90)

- Name the strongest objection or likely failure mode before expanding an idea.
  A direct request to build skips further debate.
- Verify current APIs, constraints, and terms from authoritative sources. State
  what could not be verified.
- Start with the smallest approach that delivers most of the value.
- Follow repository-local instructions and use its existing package manager.
- Test behavior before claiming completion. A successful command is not proof
  that the changed flow works.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, auth state, private sessions, or `.env`
  files.
- Proceed without confirmation when work is local, reversible, and in scope.
  Stop before destructive Git operations, deployments, remote resource
  creation, purchases, secret rotation, or deleting data without a tested
  backup.

Use the installed o90 skills for onboarding, plan-hunter planning, systematic
debugging, and verification before completion. Invoke `/adversarial-reviewer`,
`/brutal-code-reviewer`, `/debug-genius`, `/fast-impl`, or `/validator` when its
narrow role fits. These are native Cursor workflows and do not require another
runtime.

